The default implementation in java.lang.Object is approximately:

public boolean equals(Object obj) {
    return this == obj;
}

When overriding equals(), we typically compare immutable business identifiers or primary keys. A proper implementation should satisfy five properties:
1. Reflexive
2. Symmetric
3. Transitive
4. Consistent
5. x.equals(null) must return false

